course: dictionary
lesson: 14976
title: Renewal: making things new again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Renewal is a noun, a naming word for a thing or a change. It comes from the word renew, which means to make new again. Look for the word new hidden inside it: renewal is when something becomes fresh or strong again.
explain: «I took my library book to the desk for renewal, so I can keep it for three more weeks.» Renewal means making the loan last longer. Your passport, ticket or membership can need renewal too.
explain: Renewal can also mean making a place better. «The council planned urban renewal, rebuilding the old streets and parks of the town.» Old parts of a town are rebuilt and improved, so they look fresh again.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Ask: does this thing become new again, last longer, or get rebuilt? If your meaning fits the sentence, you have found it.
fact: Renewal is a noun: a renewal, or renewals.
fact: «Renewal» means making something new, fresh or strong again.
fact: «Renewal» can mean making an agreement, ticket or membership last longer.
fact: «Urban renewal» means rebuilding and improving old parts of a town.
fact: «A sense of renewal» means a feeling of being fresh and new again, such as after a good rest.
exercise: «I took my library book for renewal, so I can keep it longer.» What does renewal mean here? | Reading it out loud | Losing the book for good | Painting the cover | *Making the loan last longer
exercise: «The town started urban renewal of its old streets.» What is urban renewal? | Cleaning the rain off the roofs | Painting the sky blue | *Rebuilding and improving old parts of a town
exercise: Renewal comes from the word renew. What does renew mean? | *Make something new again | Hide something under the bed | Throw something away
test: Spring brings renewal to the forest, as new leaves push through the cold ground. What does renewal mean here? | *Fresh growth and new life again | Something ending for good | A very loud noise
test: «My membership needs renewal before June.» What does this tell you? | *The membership must be made to last longer | The membership must be cancelled for ever | Paying for a new bike
exam: «After the rain, the garden showed a sense of renewal, with bright green shoots everywhere.» What does renewal mean here? | A broken fence | A feeling of being very tired | *A feeling of being fresh and new again | Something lost
